␀Type␀umask␀Version:          %s
␀␀␀␀Author:           Mike Gleason (ncftp@ncftp.com)␀␀␀␀Archived at:      ftp://ftp.ncftp.com/ncftp/␀Library Version:  %s
␀Mar 23 2025␀Compile Date:     %s
␀Platform:         %s
␀␀?␀[optional commands]␀␀␀shows commands, or detailed help on specified commands␀ascii␀␀␀␀sets the file transfer type to ASCII text␀bgget␀[-flags] file1 [file2...]
Flags:
  -R   : Recursive.  Useful for fetching whole directories.
  -z   : Get the remote file X, and name it to Y.
  -@ <time> : Wait until <time> to do the transfer.
              It must be expressed as one of the following:
	          YYYYMMDDHHMMSS
	          "now + N hours|min|sec|days"
	          HH:MM␀␀␀collects items to download later from the remote host␀bgput␀[-flags] file1 [file2...]
Flags:
  -z   : Send the local file X, and name the remote copy to Y.
  -R   : Recursive.  Useful for sending whole directories.
  -@ <time> : Wait until <time> to do the transfer.
              It must be expressed as one of the following:
	          YYYYMMDDHHMMSS
	          "now + N hours|min|sec|days"
	          HH:MM␀␀␀collects items to upload later to the remote host␀bgstart␀[n]␀␀␀starts a ncftpbatch process to process spooled files␀binary␀sets the file transfer type to binary/image␀bookmark␀[bookmark-name-to-save-as]␀Creates or updates a bookmark using the current host and directory␀bookmarks␀[-l]␀␀␀lets you edit the settings for each bookmark␀bye␀exits NcFTP␀cat␀file1 [file2...]␀␀␀views a file from the remote host␀cd␀<directory>␀␀␀␀changes remote working directory␀chmod␀mode file1 [file2...]␀␀␀␀changes permissions for files on the remote host␀close␀␀closes the connection to the remote host␀debug␀[debug level]␀sets debug mode to level x␀delete␀␀deletes files from the remote host␀dir␀[items to list]␀␀prints a verbose directory listing␀echo␀[items to echo]␀echos back to screen␀exit␀quits NcFTP␀get␀␀␀[-flags] file1 [file2...]
Flags:
  -R   : Recursive.  Useful for fetching whole directories.
  -z   : Get the remote file X, and name it to Y.
  -a   : Get files using ASCII mode.
  -A   : Append entire remote file to the local file.
  -f   : Force overwrite (do not try to auto-resume transfers).
Examples:
  get README
  get README.*
  get "**Name with stars and spaces in it**"
  get -R new-files-directory
